            <ArticleTitle>An unusual cause of an acute abdomen--a giant colonic diverticulum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2016-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11605-010-1235-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A giant colonic diverticulum (GCD) is a rare presentation of diverticular disease of the colon that usually necessitates surgery. The case described is of a GCD that became symptomatic due to rapid enlargement caused by an intracolonic bleed. GCD usually presents with abdominal pain and a palpable periumbilical or pelvic mass. Radiological imaging shows a large gas-filled cyst associated with the colon. Surgical resection with sigmoid colectomy is usually performed to alleviate symptoms and prevent later perforation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
